*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* NAME
*       mspatch.a -- Route B spike: a global _MenuSelect ($A93D) trap patch.
*
* DESCRIPTION
*       A head patch on the MenuSelect Toolbox trap. Installed into the SYSTEM
*       heap (by msinstall, or later by an INIT) it runs in the context of every
*       application that calls MenuSelect -- including the front one. That is the
*       property Route A's background journaling lacked.
*
*       Two behaviours, chosen per call by the daemon-owned Armed word:
*         - Armed = 0 (default): transparent pass-through. JMP to the saved real
*           MenuSelect with the identical stack frame -> normal mouse tracking.
*           The daemon's own MENU: verb keeps working unchanged.
*         - Armed = 1: INTERCEPT. Return the pre-set Result (menuID<<16 | item)
*           to the caller WITHOUT entering the tracking loop -- no mouse poll, no
*           journal, no window reorder. The calling app then dispatches that menu
*           command itself. OneShot clears Armed after a single intercept.
*
*       MenuSelect is `pascal long MenuSelect(Point startPt)`. On entry via the
*       Toolbox dispatcher the stack is:
*         (SP)   return address
*         4(SP)  Point startPt   (4 bytes, param)
*         8(SP)  result slot      (4 bytes, caller-reserved)
*       Intercept returns Pascal-style: store the long into the result slot, drop
*       the param, and jump back -- leaving the result on top of stack. Only the
*       scratch registers D0/A0/A1 are touched (Pascal callee-clobber set).
*
*       Block layout (fixed offsets, shared with msinstall.c):
*         +0   BRA.S Go
*         +2   Magic   $4D53 ('MS')
*         +4   Armed   (word)  1 = intercept next call
*         +6   OneShot (word)  1 = clear Armed after one intercept
*         +8   Result  (long)  packed menuID<<16 | item to return when armed
*         +12  Real    (long)  saved real MenuSelect address (pass-through target)
*         +16  Calls   (long)  total MenuSelect calls seen
*         +20  Hits    (long)  intercepts performed
*         +24  LastRes (long)  last value returned by an intercept
*         +28  code (Go)
*
*       docs/JOURNALING_MENU_BY_NAME.md -- Route B (INIT trap patch).
*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

        CASE    OBJ
        STRING  ASIS

MSPatch         MAIN
Entry
        BRA.S   Go
Magic     DC.W    $4D53
Armed     DC.W    0
OneShot   DC.W    1
Result    DC.L    0
Real      DC.L    0
Calls     DC.L    0
Hits      DC.L    0
LastRes   DC.L    0

Go
        LEA     Entry(PC),A0            ; A0 = block base (PC-relative)
        ADDQ.L  #1,Calls-Entry(A0)      ; count every MenuSelect call
        TST.W   Armed-Entry(A0)
        BEQ.S   PassThru

        ; ---- intercept: return Result without tracking ----
        MOVE.L  Result-Entry(A0),D0
        MOVE.L  D0,LastRes-Entry(A0)
        ADDQ.L  #1,Hits-Entry(A0)
        TST.W   OneShot-Entry(A0)
        BEQ.S   NoClr
        CLR.W   Armed-Entry(A0)         ; one-shot: disarm after this call
NoClr
        MOVE.L  (SP)+,A1                ; A1 = return address; SP -> param
        ADDQ.L  #4,SP                   ; drop the 4-byte Point param; SP -> result slot
        MOVE.L  D0,(SP)                 ; store the long result into the caller's slot
        JMP     (A1)                    ; Pascal return (result left on stack)

PassThru
        MOVE.L  Real-Entry(A0),A0       ; transparent: real MenuSelect, same frame
        JMP     (A0)

        END
